.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-GET-TOPIC 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-get-topic \- show one topic's definition and counters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens get-topic
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I NAME\fR|\fIERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints one topic as JSON: its ERN, owner, retention period, its tags, how many messages it holds and how many have been published and resent through it.
.PP
A name is resolved in your session's account and namespace, so it means
your topic of that name and cannot reach another account's topic
called the same thing. A full ERN names one topic in the
installation and is what reaches another namespace's.
.PP
This is the same description
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-topics (1)
gives of each of its own, for a single topic. They share one
representation on purpose, so that a field added to a listing is in this
too rather than the two drifting apart.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR|\fIERN\fR
The topic. Required. A name is resolved in your session's account and
namespace; a full ERN reaches any namespace you are granted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The topic is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no such
topic exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli ens get-topic --topic protokollierung-topic
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-topics (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-topic-ern (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-message (1)
